# AMPLIQ — environment configuration
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in.
#
# The site builds and runs with none of these set: it sets no tracking cookies,
# links to no social profiles that do not exist, states on the page that no
# calendar is connected, and reports plainly that the contact form could not
# deliver. Nothing is faked to cover a missing value.
#
# The legal entity block is the exception. Those values are required before
# launch, but nothing on the site announces their absence: the row or sentence
# that needs one is simply left out until it is supplied.

# --- Site ---------------------------------------------------------------
# THE DOMAIN IS SET IN ONE PLACE. Everything else derives from it: the
# canonical URL, hreflang, the sitemap, Open Graph, and all three published
# email addresses. Once the final domain is bought, change this line and the
# whole site follows.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_DOMAIN="ampliq.net"

# Only if the origin differs from https://<domain> — a staging host, or a
# deployment behind a different hostname. Normally leave this unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://ampliq.net"
#
# Leave a variable OUT rather than setting it to an empty string. Both are
# handled — an unusable value falls back to https://ampliq.net and the build
# still succeeds — but a variable defined with no value in a hosting dashboard
# is a common way to think you have configured something you have not.

# The three published addresses. Each defaults to <name>@<domain> above, so
# they only need setting if a mailbox lives somewhere else.
#
#   project@  everything to do with a project: the Start-a-project flow, the
#             enquiry form, the booking, and every automated message either of
#             them sends — the notification to you, the acknowledgement to the
#             client, the booking confirmation. It is also the sender address
#             and the reply-to in those mails.
#   info@     the general company address: the footer, the Impressum, the
#             organisation record. Anything that is not about a project.
#   help@     support for existing clients.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_PROJECT_EMAIL="project@ampliq.net"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_INFO_EMAIL="info@ampliq.net"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_HELP_EMAIL="help@ampliq.net"

# No phone number is published unless one is set here. Nothing is invented.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_PHONE="+49 ..."

# --- Social -------------------------------------------------------------
# Links render only when set — an unset profile is omitted rather than linked
# to a page that does not exist.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_INSTAGRAM_URL="https://www.instagram.com/..."
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LINKEDIN_URL="https://www.linkedin.com/company/..."

# --- Email delivery -----------------------------------------------------
# One transport serves both the enquiry form and the booking confirmations.
# Until one is set, the form reports honestly that nothing was sent (HTTP 503)
# and the booking confirmation screen says no email went out.
#
# Option A — Resend. Create an API key and verify the sending domain first.
# RESEND_API_KEY="re_..."
#
# Option B — any endpoint that accepts { to, subject, html, text } as JSON.
# MAIL_ENDPOINT="https://..."
# MAIL_ENDPOINT_TOKEN="..."          # sent as a bearer token when set
#
# MAIL_FROM_EMAIL="project@ampliq.net"   # defaults to project@; must be verified
# MAIL_FROM_NAME="AMPLIQ"
# MAIL_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL="project@ampliq.net"  # where enquiries and bookings land
# MAIL_REPLY_TO="project@ampliq.net"

# --- Legal entity -------------------------------------------------------
# The five legal pages are PUBLIC and linked from the footer. They render with
# none of the variables below set: every row, sentence and chapter that depends
# on a value that has not been supplied is left out, so the documents read as
# finished rather than as a form with blanks in it. Nothing on the site says a
# value is missing, and nothing is ever invented to fill one.
#
# Setting a variable makes its row or sentence appear. Nothing else changes.
#
# These are still REQUIRED BEFORE LAUNCH — an Impressum without a business
# address is not legally sufficient, however well it reads. `npm run
# launch-check` lists which of them are still open.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_PUBLISHED="false" takes the whole section down: the routes
# answer 404 and the footer column goes. Nothing else does.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_PUBLISHED="false"
#
# Enter only what is true. If there is no GmbH, no UG, no Handelsregister entry
# and no VAT ID, leave those lines commented out — the pages will not mention
# them at all.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_COMPANY="..."             # registered name; until it is set
#                                             # the pages use the trading name
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_FORM="Einzelunternehmen"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_REPRESENTATIVE="..."      # § 18 MStV — the whole
#                                             # "Responsible for content"
#                                             # chapter waits for this
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_STREET="..."
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_POSTAL_CODE="..."         # street + postcode + city travel
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_CITY="..."                # together: the postal address and
#                                             # the AGB jurisdiction need all three
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_COUNTRY="Deutschland"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_EMAIL="..."               # defaults to the info@ address
#
# Only where they genuinely apply to the legal form:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_PHONE="..."
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_VAT_ID="DE..."
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_TAX_NUMBER="..."
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_REGISTER_COURT="..."      # both register lines together
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_REGISTER_NUMBER="..."     # add a "Register entry" chapter
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_AUTHORITY="..."
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_DPO="..."                 # defaults to the info@ address
#
# The processors the privacy policy names, once you know which they are. Each
# adds one sentence to its chapter and is absent until then, so the policy never
# names a provider this deployment does not actually use.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_HOST="..."                # e.g. "Vercel Inc."
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_EMAIL_PROCESSOR="..."     # e.g. "Resend Inc."
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_CALENDAR_PROCESSOR="..."  # e.g. "Google Ireland Limited"

# --- Booking (/start) ---------------------------------------------------
# All optional. With none of them set the booking flow still works: it shows
# the published working hours, says clearly that no calendar was consulted,
# records bookings in memory, and states that no confirmation email was sent.
# Full setup guide: docs/booking.md

# Schedule. Defaults shown; the working-hours default is Mon-Thu 09:30-12:30
# and 13:30-17:30, Fri 09:30-13:00.
# BOOKING_TIMEZONE="Europe/Berlin"
# BOOKING_SLOT_MINUTES="30"
# BOOKING_BUFFER_MINUTES="15"
# BOOKING_MINIMUM_NOTICE_HOURS="24"
# BOOKING_HORIZON_DAYS="60"
# BOOKING_STEP_MINUTES="30"
# BOOKING_WORKING_HOURS="mon-thu 09:30-12:30,13:30-17:30; fri 09:30-13:00"
# BOOKING_BLACKOUT_DATES="2026-12-24,2026-12-25"

# Calendar. Pick one, or leave unset — availability is then labelled
# "provisional" rather than presented as a live calendar check.
# Only busy times are ever read; no event details are requested or stored.
# BOOKING_CALENDAR_PROVIDER="google"   # google | microsoft | none

# Google Calendar, via OAuth 2.0 (see docs/booking.md for the full walkthrough).
#
# You never type or copy GOOGLE_OAUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN. The connect flow writes it
# for you: set the client, the calendar, the setup secret and a place to store
# it, open
#   https://ampliq.net/api/booking/google/authorize?secret=<the secret>
# once, approve the consent screen, and the token is written straight into this
# project's environment variables through the Vercel API. It is never printed,
# never logged, and never shown in the browser.
#
# On a local dev server it is written to .env.local instead, and no Vercel
# token is needed at all.
#
# Check it worked at /api/booking/google/status?secret=<the secret> — that runs
# a live free/busy call and reports the result, so you never need a log.
#
# The three /api/booking/google/* routes always exist. Without the setup secret
# they answer 503 and name what to set; with it set but not presented, 401.
#
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID="....apps.googleusercontent.com"
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET="GOCSPX-..."
# GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID="you@example.com"          # or the calendar's ID
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN="1//0g..."         # written by the flow; do not set by hand
#
# Where the flow puts the token on Vercel. Both are needed, both only during
# setup, and both should be deleted afterwards — a Vercel access token can
# change anything about the project. Free plan includes API access.
# VERCEL_TOKEN="..."                            # vercel.com/account/tokens
# VERCEL_PROJECT_ID="prj_..."                   # Project Settings -> General
# VERCEL_TEAM_ID="team_..."                     # only if the project is in a team
#
# Defaults to <site origin>/api/booking/google/callback, which in production is
# https://ampliq.net/api/booking/google/callback. Set it only when running the
# flow somewhere else — and register that exact value in Google Cloud too.
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI="http://localhost:3000/api/booking/google/callback"
#
# Opens the one-time connect flow. Unset once the refresh token is in place.
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_SETUP_SECRET="a long random string"
#
# Defaults to calendar.events + calendar.readonly. Narrow it only against
# Google's current scope list — an unknown scope fails the consent screen.
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_SCOPES="https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.readonly"
#
# GOOGLE_CALENDAR_SEND_INVITES="false"          # also let Google mail the invite

# Microsoft 365 / Outlook, via Graph client credentials.
# MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID="..."
# MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID="..."
# MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET="..."
# MICROSOFT_CALENDAR_USER="you@yourdomain.com"

# How the call happens. Set a standing meeting link and it appears in the
# confirmation email; leave it unset and the email says the details follow by
# reply, rather than inventing a link.
# BOOKING_MEETING_LINK="https://meet.google.com/..."
#
# Email for bookings uses the shared transport configured above.

# --- Analytics ----------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing loads unless an ID is set. Add a consent mechanism before enabling
# any of these — under GDPR/TTDSG they must not run before consent.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID="GTM-XXXXXXX"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID="G-XXXXXXXXXX"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID="..."
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LINKEDIN_PARTNER_ID="..."
